    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d771">

                <pb facs="0842" n="743" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg743"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">352.1115/1939a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Seville</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bay</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-10-19T19:00:00-05:00">October 19, 1936—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Please get in touch orally and informally with General Queipo de Llano and inform
                    him that the military authorities at Vigo do not permit our Consulate there to
                    send or receive cipher telegrams and that we should be grateful if appropriate
                    instructions could be transmitted at once to the authorities there directing
                    them to permit such communications freely to pass between the Department and our
                    Consul at Vigo.<anchor n="69" xml:id="d771-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d771-f1" n="69" xml:id="d771-f1-content">
                <p>By telegram November 5, 10 p.m., the Consul at Seville reported to the
                    Department: “General Queipo de Llano informed me tonight that General Franco
                    promised him during a conversation by telephone to arrange for the freedom of
                    communication with the Consul, Vigo, desired by the Department.”
                    (352.1115/2167)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
